   "claims": [
    "Standard Deviation Calculator x1 x2 You need at least two observations for sample data.",
    "The empirical rule states that for any dataset which approximates a normal distribution, about 68% of the data will fall within one standard deviation from the mean, shown in the figure below.",
    "It is written as: 𝜎 2 = 1 𝑁 ∑ 𝑖 𝑁 ( 𝑥 𝑖 − 𝜇 ) 2 σ2=N1​i∑N​(xi​−μ)2 where: 𝜎 2 σ2 - Variance; 𝜇 μ - Mean; and 𝑥 𝑖 xi​ - The ith data point out of 𝑁 N total data points.",
    "To avoid underestimating the variance of a population (and consequently, the standard deviation), we replace 𝑁 N with 𝑁 − 1 N−1 in the formulas for variance and standard deviation, when sample data is used.",
    "Calculate the mean To calculate the mean (x̄), divide the sum of all numbers by the number of data points: 𝑥 ˉ = 2 + 4 + 5 + 6 + 6 + 9 + 10 7 = 6 xˉ=72+4+5+6+6+9+10​=6.",
    "Calculate the squared differences from the mean Now that we know the mean (x̄ = 6), we will calculate the squared difference from the mean for each data point: ( 𝑥 𝑖 − 𝑥 ˉ ) 2 (xi​−xˉ)2.",
    "The calculated squared differences from the mean for all data points are shown in the table below: xi (xi - x̄)2 2 16 4 4 5 1 6 0 6 0 9 9 10 16 3.",
    "The standard deviation (s) is the square root of the variance, so our final step is: 𝑠 = 7.6667 = 2.7689 s=7.6667​=2.7689.",
    "The standard deviation of the sample dataset was 2.8.",
    "The standard deviation would then be the square root of the variance: 4.9167 ≈ 2.2 4.9167​≈2.2 Try it yourself, then check your answer with our standard deviation calculator!"
